Z||000000||Mach10||08-11-2001||02:19 PM||||I love my car. It's a blast to drive. Everyone I let try it loves it too, but complains that the brakes feel soft. I must admit, the pedal travel is longer than any of my other previous cars. They grab fine, but you have to move your foot a ways. It's not spongy, just a lot of "dead space" before the pads start biting. Is this a normal thing? I must admit that I've not driven much GM before, so I don't know if this is a design thing common to many cars, or if there is a problem in my brake system. Any comments? ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Jay||08-11-2001||02:43 PM||||This feature is known as Fiero brakes <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It is a problem on everyones Fiero.  Try putting stainless steel lines instead of the stock rubber lines.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
